title: CompoundFieldEditorTypes
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

When a tiddler has `type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki-multiple+fields`, the edit template renders one editor pane per sub-entry. The editor used for a given sub-entry is selected by the value of its `type:` header. The same selection drives the view and edit renderers of the `compound-field` procedure, see [[CompoundFieldHeaders]].

! Built-in editor types

|!`type:` value |!Editor |
|//(absent)// |single-line text input |
|`multiline` |full `$edit` widget with toolbar and per-pane preview |
|`date` |HTML `<input type="date">` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) |
|`date-time` |HTML `<input type="datetime-local">` |
|`email` |HTML `<input type="email">` |
|`phone` |HTML `<input type="tel">` |
|`url` |HTML `<input type="url">` |
|`color` |HTML `<input type="color">` |
|`option-A-B[-C…]` |radio buttons, one per dash-separated label, plus a `none` |
|`select-KEY` |dropdown sourced from the `KEY` metadata header (see below) |
|`relation-TAG` |picker over the tiddlers tagged `TAG`, stored as a [[title list|Title List]] |
|`template-prefix` |the value names a template prefix; `<prefix>-ViewTemplate` and `<prefix>-EditTemplate` render the field |

! Extending: `option-…` (N radio buttons)

The string after `option-` is split on `-` and each part becomes a radio button. The widget also adds a `none` button at the end.

```
title: priority
type: option-low-medium-high

medium
```

Anything after `option-` is treated as data; no separate definition is needed. The labels become both the displayed text and the stored value. Dashes inside an option are not supported because `-` is the separator.

! Extending: `select-…` (dropdown sourced from a metadata header)

The `select-KEY` form looks for a metadata header named `KEY` on the //same sub-entry// (or on the [[schema|CompoundSchema]] that applies to the tiddler). The header's value is split as a [[title list|Title List]] to produce the dropdown options.

```
title: role
type: select-roles
roles: [[Developer]] [[Designer]] [[Team Lead]] CEO

Designer
```

The lookup goes through the `compound-field-meta` [[filter operator|Filter Operators]], so the option list can live on a shared schema:

```
title: ContactTemplate
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki-multiple+fields

title: role
type: select-roles
roles: [[Developer]] [[Designer]] [[Team Lead]] CEO

```

```
title: Alice
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki-multiple+fields
inherit-schema: ContactTemplate

title: role

Designer
```

`Alice` does not define `roles`. `inherit-schema` makes `ContactTemplate` her [[schema|CompoundSchema]], and the editor reads the option list from it.

! Adding a brand-new editor type

Both renderers live in the `compound-field` procedure in `$:/core/macros/compound-field`. To define a wholly new editor (e.g. a slider, a map field):

# Add a new `<%elseif [<_type>match[…]] %>` branch (or `prefix[…]` branch, for parameterised types) to its edit block and, if the type needs a custom display, to its view block.
# If the new type takes parameters in the same metadata-driven style as `select-`, read a metadata header via `compound-field-meta` so the template can carry the configuration.

The edit-template's type-selector dropdown is also extensible: any `prefix[option-]` or `prefix[select-]` values the wiki already contains are added to the dropdown automatically (via `compound-field-types[]`). To surface a new prefix in the dropdown the same way, add an analogous `<$list>` clause to the `compound-type-selector` procedure.
